# No Cursor agent in git commits

Do **not** include Cursor, Cursor Agent, or `cursoragent@cursor.com` as a commit co-author.

- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any similar Cursor/agent trailer) to commit messages.
- If a commit message is auto-injected with that trailer, remove it before pushing (amend only when the commit is still local and created in this session).
- Commit messages should credit only the human author / repo owner.
